{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_ed7ea7cd91c6f6cbdde6e56392485b9be8a95b4771581305fdd92abfdc23dc85"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: the README's Development section lists npm scripts for building everything, CLI watch mode, running tests, and test watch mode; contributor notes specify Vitest for tests and separate build pipelines (tsc for CLI, Vite for dashboard, esbuild for host)."}],"claim_ids":["clm_ed7ea7cd91c6f6cbdde6e56392485b9be8a95b4771581305fdd92abfdc23dc85"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T02:16:19Z","created_by_operation":"op_faf01875fecc4d4fa094d81c38ae5cd6","id":"pg_0f0e090aee255925a474d1c5942798a6","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/marsz42-awel-claude-md-3687fea3fa73-d1c5942798a6.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_3a97db4ad83f57188d513f4958ea8d22"],"title":"MarsZ42/Awel/CLAUDE.md @ 3687fea3fa73","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:16:19Z","updated_by_operation":"op_faf01875fecc4d4fa094d81c38ae5cd6"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_013a36dbe9fd8f2c84bcf87e95975daa11a994d83c7d0102e8caa22ed0bac309"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The CLI exposes two commands: `awel create` to scaffold a new Next.js project in creation mode, and `awel dev` with options `-p/--port` (default 3000), `-v/--verbose` for LLM stream events on stderr, and `--no-open`."},{"claim_ids":["clm_05c8cc81de4879fcc1f6df75a57005dbd6942278a2a7fa10d61c3177adb4fdf3"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Model switching appears to be supported at runtime via a dropdown in the dashboard header, with at least one configured provider required for Awel to function."},{"claim_ids":["clm_3f635834af19b65b5eaadf1046cf9df56e3c8749476d5b853e6ffd85acf98195"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The dashboard offers an element inspector for attaching selected DOM elements as prompt context, a screenshot annotator, image attachments, plan approval, per-session undo of agent file changes, and diff review before accepting changes."},{"claim_ids":["clm_4744c115b07d63f708e42752d86cf58a17c9e3d02fe7791eacd2156b2728097e"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The agent has tools for file read/write/edit, shell commands, code search, web search/fetch, plan proposal, user questions, dev-server restart, todo tracking, and persistent memory, with file edits and shell commands subject to optional user confirmation."},{"claim_ids":["clm_7cdbe55d1ac966914171516d14b699b1e8932f21cf72a72d198431d10e6edfb8"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Awel is built on the Vercel AI SDK and supports multiple providers configured via environment variables, including Anthropic, OpenAI, Google AI, MiniMax, Zhipu, Vercel Gateway, OpenRouter, and a Claude CLI in PATH."},{"claim_ids":["clm_85ba173b72b3e1aeebebed01537054c397dab540a366d809f8301dfc08af863d"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Awel targets Next.js developers, letting them converse with an AI agent that can read, write, and edit project files from an embedded dashboard during development."},{"claim_ids":["clm_91f9abca059948acdee6f00ba63503a79de03360dfda391c76c9656a0aa8b12d"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"HMR/WebSocket traffic is proxied through transparently and paused while the agent edits files, to prevent hot-reload interference."},{"claim_ids":["clm_9a36544b8c582d4ea382568cd8ef649be1264e01f362cf5b15642c3449b33f18"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The agent includes a Memory tool to store and retrieve persistent project knowledge, and the product advertises saving and recalling project-specific knowledge across sessions."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a59d28db92b902eacfc1bed2e8eb07a6d2a0170ca78b5538f1edb5ff9a38a86b"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Awel runs a proxy on port 3001 in front of the Next.js dev server on port 3000, intercepts HTML responses to inject a script, and opens a full-screen chat dashboard in an iframe from a floating Shadow DOM button."},{"claim_ids":["clm_bdc8b859495abc0bba5cf243335f5e270e5b03b85da6cb009d095f2bf7ebb954"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Claude Code models run in 'YOLO mode', automatically approving all file edits and shell commands without confirmation; a warning is displayed when such a model is selected."},{"claim_ids":["clm_ed7ea7cd91c6f6cbdde6e56392485b9be8a95b4771581305fdd92abfdc23dc85"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: the README's Development section lists npm scripts for building everything, CLI watch mode, running tests, and test watch mode; contributor notes specify Vitest for tests and separate build pipelines (tsc for CLI, Vite for dashboard, esbuild for host)."}],"claim_ids":["clm_013a36dbe9fd8f2c84bcf87e95975daa11a994d83c7d0102e8caa22ed0bac309","clm_05c8cc81de4879fcc1f6df75a57005dbd6942278a2a7fa10d61c3177adb4fdf3","clm_3f635834af19b65b5eaadf1046cf9df56e3c8749476d5b853e6ffd85acf98195","clm_4744c115b07d63f708e42752d86cf58a17c9e3d02fe7791eacd2156b2728097e","clm_7cdbe55d1ac966914171516d14b699b1e8932f21cf72a72d198431d10e6edfb8","clm_85ba173b72b3e1aeebebed01537054c